Archive source-metadata derivative: independent source review, 2026-10-15

Disposition: SOURCE-ONLY APPROVAL; no blocking implementation issue found in
the inspected five-file overlay. This is not test, integration, original,
browser, product-parity, security or performance acceptance.

Scope read: derivative README and all five overlay files; frozen793 candidate
server.mjs, operation-budget.mjs, original-aes-test-helper.mjs, and base README.
A read-only unified diff directly compared both server files. No stage edits,
application execution, syntax check, tests, builds, bootstrap, service start,
bulk hashing or whole-stage census were performed. This note is the only
reviewer-authored file.

Base authority identifiers were supplied by the parent and repeated in the
overlay README. They were not independently rehashed here:
manifest a37d03df0fdf4ef53fcd8e5bbcca7aab465b6329810ca9cab33210417af0825e
validation 456bb217f78ffb2ceb9ccf901a3e22bda726bd45bbbb53dd07a744e5d56ae11e
base server 232d0c94e0b38da741ba751d7dbe39e1fd51da0c5d1a3511b2aae16ab36ba9c6

Findings supporting source-only approval:

1. Paths cross the native process boundary only in bounded UTF-8 stdin JSON.
   The EncodedCommand is a constant UTF-16LE program. No path or password is
   interpolated into program text or command arguments. execFile uses an
   explicit installed Windows PowerShell path, shell:false and windowsHide.

2. JS validates an absolute root, confined absolute source paths, unique
   case-folded paths, boolean source types and bounded request size. The
   child repeats confinement and root-to-target reparse/type checks using
   literal paths. JS correlates every returned row by ordered index, path
   and type, preventing reordered or substituted native observations.

3. Native UTC strings are correlated with independent decimal milliseconds
   at 100-nanosecond precision before reducing to the existing whole-ms
   archive contract. Negative fractional milliseconds are represented by
   signed decimal ticks; the date parser's whole-ms value plus the final
   four fractional digits gives the matching negative-epoch ticks.
   Invalid/normalized dates and inconsistent values refuse safely.

4. Directory and single-file creation await validated metadata before any
   output-parent mkdir, container commit or archive write. Existing size
   checks and no-link walk remain. Native parse/transport/disappearance
   failures therefore occur before output-directory creation. Reparse and
   concurrent content/metadata replacement races remain explicitly disclosed.

5. Non-Windows dates use the same stat objects captured before content reads.
   Windows dates intentionally come from the native batch after content
   reads; access-time updates may therefore be observed. The documentation
   states this change and the non-atomic source-capture limitation.

6. The direct server diff has six localized hunks: metadata import and queue
   declaration relocation; collection signature; collected date plumbing;
   run signature; single-file metadata plumbing; handler factory/default
   singleton. Date/container/extraction/crypto implementations outside those
   explicit regions are unchanged in the compared files. The default handler
   retains the original per-workspace serialized queue and password deletion.
   Exact byte-hash/inverse and complete-base authentication remain cloud
   composition checks; no whole793 identity claim follows from this diff.

7. MIT notice is scoped to the independent new metadata adapter and tests;
   the overlay explicitly retains all frozen source-assisted AES/LZMA and
   existing server licensing. No original binary is added to the overlay.

Bounds and acceptance limitations:

- Native input is capped at 32 MiB, output at 64 MiB, source count at 10,000,
  and the process at 15 seconds. The same caller OperationBudget is checked
  immediately before/after the metadata await. Expiry prevents archive commit,
  but a child is not preempted at a smaller caller-supplied maxTimeMs. This is
  cooperative bounded I/O, not a strict wall-clock operation deadline.
- Nine authored test groups were read but not run. They include Unicode and
  shell-looking paths, decimal/UTC checks, 1969/2106/2107 native fixtures,
  plain ZIP/plain and encrypted7Z restoration, refusal paths and a junction.
- New tests do not explicitly exercise source/request/response caps, actual
  native timeout, or expiry while an awaited metadata batch is held. Fresh
  cloud-only controls should accompany any acceptance claim about those bounds.
- Exact pre/post source identities, original-prerequisite acquisition and
  original-process accounting, native raw observations, the base151 regression
  selection and current actual-browser acceptance remain separate work.
- Frozen793, its old151 receipt and the live Archive app were not changed.
